-- ==========================================================================
-- 0014 - the November 2023 run sheets: the weekly pattern
--
-- Generated by data/build_nov23_import.py from the two spreadsheets in data/.
-- Do not hand-edit: change the sheet or the generator and regenerate.
--
-- What the sheets DO say, and is therefore reliable here:
--   the customer list, addresses, what to collect or deliver, access notes
--   and contacts, which weekdays each customer is visited, and whether they
--   are weekly, fortnightly, monthly or on call.
--
-- What the sheets do NOT say, and is a guess for the office to correct:
--
--   * WHICH DRIVER. Split by suburb: the west on Kemu's van, the city and
--     inner east and south on Darren's, Werribee and Wyndham on Keith's,
--     Geelong on the truck. Nothing in the sheet supports this beyond
--     geography. Moving a customer to another run is remove-then-add in the
--     Runs screen, so expect that to be the bulk of the tidying up.
--
--   * THE ORDER WITHIN A DAY. Alphabetical, because the master sheet is
--     alphabetical. The one exception is Kemu's Thursday, whose real running
--     order came off his own sheet and is already loaded - left untouched,
--     with the master sheet's extra Thursday stops appended behind it.
--
-- Re-runnable. Customers match on external_ref; stops are skipped when the
-- same customer already sits on that run and weekday.
-- ==========================================================================

-- -- the weekly pattern -----------------------------------------------------
-- Kemu's Thursday closing marker moves to the back so his proven running
